WEBVTT

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.490
There.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.890
All done setting up our tents!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.020
The tarp really completes it, huh?

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.250
Really makes you feel like a veteran camper.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.200
I'm amazed you found such 
a great place, though, Aki.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.420
Right?

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.010
It's super busy here in 
the summertime, though.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.590
It's so quiet.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.900
And the air is nice and clean.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.010
Yeah.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.370
Winter camping is the best.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:23.990
<b>(2) Episode 6 
Cape Ohmama in Winter</b>

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.740
So, how do I put this together?

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.990
It has instructions on the chair itself.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.000
Let's see...

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.250
Put this together first,

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.100
then insert the frame into 
the corners of the seat...

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.510
Compact Outdoor Chair
12,600 yen

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.590
It's done!

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.220
That was super easy.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.760
It's well-built for something so compact.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:46.020
It's held together with elastic 
cords, like those tent poles.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.520
It feels like it's hugging me.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.450
I'm so glad I bought this.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.160
I'm all done over here, too.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:03.030
Compact Chair ×2
 Hammock

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.830
How does it feel to lie in it?

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.040
Pretty comfy.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.850
Though it's more like a deck 
chair than a hammock.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.270
Wanna give it a try, Ena?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:15.290
Yeah!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.990
This makes you not want to move.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.400
Can I try it, too?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.300
Sure.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.350
You're right.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.160
This is so nice.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.570
Right?

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:32.710
I just realized they're different chairs.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:33.710
Yeah.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.770
With front legs
10,360 yen

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.180
It's more expensive to buy two,

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.070
so I got one of the cheaper kind
that doesn't have front legs.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.070
Without front legs
7,700 yen

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.250
It's not as stable, but I'm 
only putting my feet in it.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.140
Let's start prepping the hot pot.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.580
Cut it out.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.580
Okay, let's take our chairs and coffee sets...

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.180
and go chill at the end of the cape!

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.870
Yeah!

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.340
"Woof"?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.870
It's a corgi.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.430
When did it get here?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.800
Hey! Choko!

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.160
Don't do that!

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.940
I'm sorry. I looked away for one second, and...

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.730
Oh, it's all right.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.220
Wow...

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.900
So you're camping with your doggy, huh?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.740
Yes.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.160
We have a chihuahua at home,

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.480
but he doesn't like the cold, 
so we're waiting for it to get warmer.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.500
Oh?

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.620
There, there!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.250
So this is Choco-chan?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.510
Yes.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.260
Not "choco" as in chocolate, 
but rather "choko" as in ochoko.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.260
Ochoko?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.510
Ohmama Nishiki

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.510
Like for sake?

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.000
My family owns a sake shop.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.260
Oh...

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.750
Ochoko-chan!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.960
Well, see you around.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.730
Sure.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.870
Bye.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.400
Bye-bye, Choko-chan.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.180
A drone?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.180
I think it's more of an RC plane.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.180
Hobbyists, huh?

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.320
All right, we're here.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:41.690
Mountain camping is nice,
but lakeside camping is great, too.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.140
Isn't it?

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.820
It's especially relaxing when you have a chair...

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.800
I'll lend you one.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.910
Are you sure?

00:05:54.910 --> 00:06:01.460
I feel like a horrible person using two
when you're sitting on the ground.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.860
Thanks.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.550
You're such a good person, Aki.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.970
Such a good person.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.340
Aw, enough already!
You're embarrassing me, dang it.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.190
Oh, I know!

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:16.390
We should share all the fun we're having
with the poor girls who're stuck at work.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.950
Jeez, you're evil after all.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.600
A demon.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.210
You two are all smiles yourselves.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.110
<b>camping at Lake Yamanaka</b>

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.370
My battery's down to 9%?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.620
You didn't charge it before we left?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.010
I thought it was full this morning.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.430
Maybe I took too many photos.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.970
Mine's completely dead already.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.260
Huh?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.450
Wait, mine's under 20%, too. What gives?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:55.940
I think I've heard somewhere before that 
batteries drain faster when it's cold.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.240
Guess we should turn them off for now.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.400
Good call.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.530
All right!

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.760
Let's lift our spirits with some tea.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.150
Agreed!

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.070
What are you making, Aki-chan?

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.410
It's a cocktail called 
"hot buttered rum cow."

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.170
Cocktail? As in liquor?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.620
Don't worry. It's non-alcoholic.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.150
My coworker taught it to me.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.430
Perks of working at a liquor store, huh?

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.180
It's good.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.820
The cinnamon is relaxing.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.190
Right?

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>There.</i>

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.680
<i>Next, I have to deal with the portable grill.</i>

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.980
Mom, do we have any pipe cleaner?

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.990
<i>Grandpa taught me how to clean burnt grills.</i>

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.530
<i>Now the soot should float to the top.</i>

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.760
Chill camping at Lake Yamanaka

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.000
Lake Yamanaka, huh?

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.280
Weather Information

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.280
Lake Yamanaka...

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:21.410
H-Hey, is it just me, 
or is it getting really cold?

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.420
Y-Yeah...

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:26.440
Should we head back and start the campfire?

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:30.600
A-Aki-chan, there's ice in my mug.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.670
What? Seriously?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.800
Look.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.430
<b>Saturday, Jan. 20th</b>

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.800
<b>Lake Yamanaka Village</b>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.810
<b>Lake Yamanaka Village</b>

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.360
Minus two?!

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.440
It's only 4:30!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:50.320
It wasn't this cold during our
 Christmas camp, was it?

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.540
No, it wasn't.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:52.940
Wait... Of course!

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:57.620
The campsite in Asagiri was 
600 meters above sea level.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.900
Lake Yamanaka is almost 1,000 meters.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.280
Of course it's colder here.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:07.210
If it's minus two right now, 
how cold will it be tonight?

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.210
Weather Information

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:10.750
My battery died.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:14.000
Mine's dead, too...

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:24.310
I think we got in a little over our heads once 
we started getting used to winter camping...

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.020
Sorry!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.970
I never looked up the weather or anything.

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:35.760
For now, let's just think about 
what we can do. Okay, Aki?

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.650
Yeah.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:39.020
O-Okay.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.190
We need to warm up.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.660
Okay, first we need the hot pot!

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:47.290
We'll have hot pot and warm 
ourselves up from the inside.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:50.980
At the same time, we'll warm up 
from the outside with a campfire.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.810
Uh-huh.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:55.370
And before we get cold, 
we'll get in our sleeping bags,

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.800
throw our coats and blankets on top, 
and sleep next to each other.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.910
It might be warmer if we put 
hand warmers in our sleeping bags.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.150
Oh, good idea!

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.680
I have one, too.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.180
Those are regular ones...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.310
Regular ones?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:13.190
You need the hot ones, or else
 they'll get cold halfway through.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.190
<b>Kachikachi Mountain <i>Hot Hand Warmers</i></b>

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.500
I didn't bring enough to share, though.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.190
Okay, I'll go buy some 
from the convenience store!

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:23.090
Also, we could put some cardboard
under our sleeping pads.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.110
We could put some on top, too.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.700
Okay. I'll go ask for some.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.170
Wait, we haven't bought firewood yet, have we?

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.030
Oh, yeah.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.210
We need the campfire while we're 
making the hot pot, or we'll freeze.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.910
All right, I'm making a dash 
for the convenience store.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.870
You guys buy firewood and start the hot pot!

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:42.030
Got it!

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.970
Stay safe, Aki.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.080
<i>Hand warmers...</i>

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.280
<i>Cardboard...</i>

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:51.170
<i>Hand warmers...</i>

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:52.610
<i>Cardboard...</i>

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.220
<i>The convenience store is so far!</i>

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.050
The admin building's closed...

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.920
D-Do you think we're in trouble?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.750
Wait, was that the manager's car?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.870
It was!

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.970
Where will we get firewood?

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:32.030
Is there anything we can burn instead?

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:33.340
Like twigs?

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.920
Good idea. Let's look around.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:43.260
Not a single one...

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.780
Hey, it's you girls.

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:56.110
Here. Come on in.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.790
Thank you.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.050
Welcome.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.200
Good evening.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.580
Wow, it's so warm.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:11.810
I know.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.530
We have a wood stove, after all.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.070
Thank goodness for wood stoves.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.800
Thank you so much for saving us.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.790
Don't worry about it. Our tent is big enough.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:26.700
Besides...

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.420
You'd be goners if we'd left you out there.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.210
Right, Choko?

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.330
That's not funny...

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.770
Go on. Have a seat.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:36.580
Okay.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.610
It's a plane.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.220
Were you the one flying 
that RC model around noon?

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.170
Yeah, that was me. Were you watching?

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.470
We were watching from our chairs.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.180
Yeah.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.600
You were, huh?

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:55.790
I'm in a seaplane hobby club.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.750
We come up to Lake Yamanaka 
every now and then to fly them.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.860
Wow.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.180
We're about to have motsu hot pot.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.360
Have you girls already had dinner?

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.840
We were about to make hot pot, too.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.610
In that case, why don't we...

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.380
10-pack
780 yen

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.380
<b>Kachikachi Mountain <i>Hot Hand Warmers</i></b>

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.380
Value pack of high-temp hand warmers!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.380
Six sheets
0 yen

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.380
And cardboard!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.910
Wait, where are they?

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.890
Hey! Inuko!

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.280
Ena! Where are you?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.900
Aki! Over here!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.560
It's so warm...

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:50.160
Welcome back.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:54.090
Ah, I see. This lady's been 
helping you guys, huh?

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:57.160
Thanks, Aki. It must have been cold.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.420
Actually, nah, not really.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.280
Come on in, young lady. 
Warm up by the stove.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.010
Thank you.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.670
Kiritanpo?

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:14.470
We decided to have a hot pot party with them.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.300
Oh, yeah?

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.470
We're making motsu hot pot over here.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.810
Nice!

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.840
And we have ramen to finish with, too.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.770
That's awesome!

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.070
You've forgotten about our 
kiritanpo hot pot, haven't you?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.930
Wanna help make them?

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:31.070
Sure.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.890
Ohgaki-san!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:37.310
Inuyama-san!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.370
Saitou-san!

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:51.380
<i>These are their tents, aren't they?</i>

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.780
<i>No one's here...</i>

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.210
<i>They aren't picking up, either.</i>

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.100
Don't tell me...

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:12.720
What are you doing?

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.930
I thought you had somewhere to be, Sensei.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.370
Yes, but...

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:25.630
I was working at school when 
I got a message from Shima-san.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:33.090
Sensei, Chiaki and the others are camping 
at Lake Yamanaka right now.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:37.640
It gets down to 15 below there 
sometimes. I'm quite worried.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.590
What?! Lake Yamanaka?

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.640
They aren't picking up 
for some reason, either.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.610
So I got worried and came to check on you.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:48.770
Like Shima-san said, after all,
you wouldn't pick up.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:54.280
Actually, our phone batteries died. 
Maybe because of the cold...

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.360
So that's why...

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:01.540
Listen well, girls.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.740
The elevation varies greatly in this area.

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:09.640
A slight change in location can mean
 a drastic change in temperature.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:15.050
This is hardly the appropriate gear 
for Lake Yamanaka in the winter.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:19.050
You need to do your research 
and be thoroughly prepared.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.040
Winter camping can be very dangerous.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.610
This could have been an incident.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:29.310
We're sorry.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.430
I'm sorry, too.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.680
I knew you were going camping.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:40.580
I should have asked where you were going.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:46.070
Please talk to me whenever you go camping.

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:48.210
I'm your advisor now, after all.

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:50.040
Sensei...

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:54.840
I'm so glad you're all safe.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.790
Now... I'll get in touch with 
Shima-san and let her know.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.100
Sensei!

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.880
Sensei, why don't you join us?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.620
We've got some damn fine sake.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.100
Yeah, hello? Shima-san?

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.940
It's me!

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.740
Let's get started with the hot pot, too.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.670
Thank you for all your help.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:02.730
Thank you, too.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:05.290
That was a fun hot pot party.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.800
Please be sure to stop by 
our shop if you're ever in Itou.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.290
We have that Izu sake you loved, Sensei.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.550
Yesshir! Ah shall be there!

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:19.100
You're so drunk, Sensei.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.410
N'ahm not!

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.530
So cold!

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:13.080
We made it through the night. 
Thanks for worrying about us, Rin

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.290
Thanks a bunch

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:18.560
I'll never forget this!!

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.570
You'd better bring me gifts from Lake Yamanaka

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:47.300
<b><i>Car
Wax</i></b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.300
<i>It's gotten pretty dirty.</i>

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:49.580
<i>Time to give it a wash.</i>

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:59.060
Hey, all done with work?

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:01.960
Yeah, I just finished.

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.340
<i>How's the new job?</i>

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:07.350
My coworkers are nice, 
and talking with customers is fun.

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.280
I get tasty leftovers, too.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.340
<i>Really?</i>

00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:14.350
<i>Hey, anyway, there's something 
I wanted to talk to you about.</i>

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:15.580
There is?

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:17.800
Yeah.

00:23:18.490 --> 00:23:24.040
The thing is... I want to try 
solo camping like you do.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:35.260
Next Episode

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>Nadeshiko's Solo Camp Planning</b>

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...
